  <id>2133844</id>
  <releasedate>2024-11-06</releasedate>
  <summary>&lt;p>This is the KWin port of the Glitch effect of the Burn-My-Windows GNOME Shell extension. &lt;a href="https://github.com/Schneegans/Burn-My-Windows#%EF%B8%8F-installation-kwin">You can find a list of all Burn-My-Windows effects which are currently available for KWin on GitHub.&lt;/a>&lt;br />&lt;br />&lt;b>This effect requires at least KWin 6.0.0. Also, if the color picker widgets in the settings of any of the Burn-My-Windows effects do not work, you may have to install the package &amp;quot;libkf6widgetsaddons-dev&amp;quot; (Kubuntu, KDE Neon, etc) or &amp;quot;kf6-kwidgetaddons-devel&amp;quot; (Fedora, OpenSuse, etc).&lt;/b> If you encounter a bug or have a feature request, please open an issue on &lt;a href="https://github.com/Schneegans/Burn-My-Windows/issues">GitHub&lt;/a>!&lt;br />&lt;br />&lt;i>IMHO, there are many things which could be done to improve the KWin port of the extension. However, since I am not using KDE as a daily driver, I would appreciate it very much if someone volunteers to work on this port! I am happily receiving pull requests...&lt;/i>&lt;/p></summary>
  <changelog></changelog>
  <preview>https://images.pling.com/img/00/00/67/07/53/2133844/glitch.gif</preview>
